A billing report shows some line totals as `0.00` for accounts that certainly have charges.

```csharp
public decimal RateFor(string planCode)
{
    return _plans
        .Where(p => p.Code == planCode)
        .Select(p => p.RatePerHour)
        .FirstOrDefault();
}

// caller
decimal total = hours * RateFor(account.PlanCode);
```

No exception is thrown and the method never returns null. What is wrong, and what should it do instead?

solution.code:
function projectFields(row, fields) {
  const out = {};
  for (const field of fields) {
    if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(row, field)) {
      out[field] = row[field];
    }
  }
  return out;
}

